{
  "id": "T-1665",
  "created_at": 1791242447.255881,
  "parent": "T-1661",
  "role": "review",
  "tier": "sonnet",
  "complexity": 7,
  "title": "review: with-tokens.sh: remove the WITH_TOKENS_ALLOWLIST override (any agent could allowlist any token)",
  "spec": "Security fix for scripts/with-tokens.sh (merged in PR 41, 3941301). The allowlist path can be overridden with the\nenvironment variable WITH_TOKENS_ALLOWLIST (scripts/with-tokens.sh:26). Any agent can write its own allowlist in /tmp,\nset that variable and receive every token in the store, which defeats the human-owned allowlist entirely.\nFound by the Planner on 2026-10-05 after merge; the security review T-1656 missed it.\n\nChange:\n1. scripts/with-tokens.sh always reads <repo root>/.orchestrator/token-allowlist.txt, where repo root is the parent of\n   the script's own directory (as today). Remove the WITH_TOKENS_ALLOWLIST override completely. If the variable is set\n   in the environment, refuse with exit 3 \"with-tokens: WITH_TOKENS_ALLOWLIST is not supported\" so a caller relying on it\n   notices.\n2. Keep WITH_TOKENS_F_SH (a fake f.sh only yields fake values; no privilege gain) but update the header comment to say\n   it exists for tests only.\n3. Update the header comment: the allowlist location is fixed and protected by protected-paths.txt.\n\nTests (tests/test_with_tokens.py): stop using WITH_TOKENS_ALLOWLIST. Each test copies scripts/with-tokens.sh into a temp\ndirectory laid out as <tmp>/scripts/with-tokens.sh and writes <tmp>/.orchestrator/token-allowlist.txt, then runs the copy.\nKeep all eight existing tests green with that layout and add:\n- test_allowlist_override_env_refused: WITH_TOKENS_ALLOWLIST set to a temp file listing b-key -> exit 3, the message\n  above, no value in output, command not run.\n- test_allowlist_location_fixed: a second allowlist elsewhere is ignored; only <root>/.orchestrator/token-allowlist.txt counts.\nRun: uv run python -m pytest -q tests/test_with_tokens.py (or unittest). Commit on the task branch.\n",
  "inputs": [
    "T-1662"
  ],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_with_tokens.py: the eight existing tests plus test_allowlist_override_env_refused and test_allowlist_location_fixed pass",
    "scripts/with-tokens.sh reads only <repo root>/.orchestrator/token-allowlist.txt and refuses when WITH_TOKENS_ALLOWLIST is set",
    "No change under .claude/hooks or to .orchestrator/protected-paths.txt"
  ],
  "scope": [
    "scripts/with-tokens.sh",
    "tests/test_with_tokens.py"
  ],
  "depends_on": [],
  "constraints": {
    "read_only": true,
    "budget_turns": 20,
    "timeout_s": 900
  },
  "status": "done",
  "assigned_to": "claude:A",
  "worktree": "/Users/k3ntaw/code/orchestrator/wt/T-1665",
  "codex_thread": null,
  "result": {
    "summary": "Acceptance is met. The override is removed. Setting WITH_TOKENS_ALLOWLIST (even to an empty value, via the `+set` check) exits 3 with the required message before anything else runs. The allowlist path is fixed to <repo root>/.orchestrator/token-allowlist.txt. The header comments are updated as specified. The two new tests exist and are not vacuous: the first checks the exit code, the message, empty stdout and that the command did not run, and also checks --list. The second checks that other allowlists are ignored. The diff touches only the two scoped files, not .claude/hooks or protected-paths.txt. I read the diff only and did not run the tests. The gate reports one attempt with no reds.",
    "verdict": "approve",
    "comments": [
      {
        "path": "scripts/with-tokens.sh",
        "line": 33,
        "issue": "The repo root comes from the script's own location, so an agent can copy the script to <tmp>/scripts/with-tokens.sh, write its own <tmp>/.orchestrator/token-allowlist.txt and run that copy. That recreates the bypass this task closes, unless the real f helper path is fixed and checks the caller. Not in this task's spec, but follow it up (for example, have the f helper or token store enforce the allowlist).",
        "severity": "med"
      },
      {
        "path": "scripts/with-tokens.sh",
        "line": 19,
        "issue": "WITH_TOKENS_F_SH is kept as the spec requires. An agent could point it at a script it controls, which gets the token ids and the process environment. Low risk because it only receives ids, not real values.",
        "severity": "low"
      }
    ],
    "packet_version": "f912a3549281",
    "confidence": 0.0,
    "provenance": [
      "repo"
    ]
  },
